1. Definitions

1.1. "Software" means the Canwu software, source code, object code,
documentation, and other materials distributed with this License, including
modifications and derivative works of those materials to the extent they are
derived from the Software.

1.2. "Licensor" means the copyright owner identified above or any successor
that lawfully owns the relevant rights in the Software.

1.3. "You" or "Licensee" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights
under this License.

1.4. "Affiliate" means any entity that directly or indirectly controls, is
controlled by, or is under common control with a party. "Control" means the
direct or indirect power to direct management or policies, whether through
ownership, voting rights, contract, or otherwise.

1.5. "Product Family" means one product and all commercially related versions
that are substantially the same product or share a common commercial identity,
purpose, user experience, or monetization program. A Product Family includes,
without limitation, its editions, platform releases, ports, downloadable
content, expansions, subscriptions, season passes, in-app purchases, paid
add-ons, and other monetization tied to substantially the same product.

Materially distinct standalone products are normally separate Product Families.
A different name, edition, publisher, storefront, platform, distribution
method, subsidiary, or controlled entity does not by itself create a separate
Product Family.

1.6. "Independent Work" means code, content, data, or other material that is not
copied or derived from the Software, even when it interoperates with, links to,
embeds, or is distributed with the Software.

1.7. "Commercial Product" means a Product Family that is sold, licensed,
offered by subscription, supported by advertising or in-app purchases, used to
provide a paid service, or otherwise offered or operated with the purpose of
generating Product Revenue.

1.8. "Product Revenue" has the meaning given in Section 7.

1.9. "Product Revenue Year" means a consecutive twelve-month measurement
period for a Product Family. The first Product Revenue Year begins on the first
date the Product Family generates Product Revenue while incorporating or using
the Software. Each following Product Revenue Year begins immediately after the
previous one ends. If the Software is first added to an already commercialized
Product Family, the first Product Revenue Year begins on the date that Product
Family first commercially uses the Software.

Each Product Revenue Year is divided into four consecutive three-month reporting
quarters beginning on the first day of that Product Revenue Year. A transfer,
restructuring, publisher change, creation or use of an Affiliate, or change in
distribution method does not restart or shorten the Product Revenue Year for the
purpose of avoiding royalties.

1.10. "Third-Party Materials" means software, fonts, data, documentation, or
other material owned by someone other than Licensor and distributed with,
linked by, or used through the Software under a separate license or notice.
Third-Party Materials are not part of the Software for purposes of this License.
They remain governed by their own licenses, which control solely for those
materials if their terms conflict with this License.

