14. Material Breach and Termination

If Licensee materially breaches this License, Licensor may provide written
notice describing the breach. Licensee has thirty days after receiving notice
to cure the breach, including by stopping the violation, providing overdue
statements, and paying overdue amounts as applicable. If Licensee does not fully
cure within that period, the licenses granted under this License terminate at
the end of the cure period upon written notice from Licensor.

After termination, Licensee must stop exercising rights under this License,
except as necessary to wind down distribution in an orderly manner or as
otherwise agreed in writing. Termination does not revoke licenses already
received directly under this License by compliant downstream recipients.

Accrued reporting, audit, royalty, payment, confidentiality, ownership,
disclaimer, limitation-of-liability, governing-law, and enforcement obligations
survive termination. Termination does not excuse Product Revenue earned or
royalties accrued before termination.

